<title>USA: Loews Corp Q4 net per share falls to $2.15.</title>
<headline>Loews Corp Q4 net per share falls to $2.15.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.15		    $6.32</p>
<p> Net			247,800		  745,100</p>
<p> Revs		   5,137,000		5,495,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 115,000		  117,800</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			 $11.91		   $14.98</p>
<p> Net		    1,383,900		1,765,700</p>
<p> Revs		  16,628,400	     15,521,800</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 116,200		  117,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Loews reports Q4 net realized investment losses of $8.6 million, or $0.07 per share, compared to $558.0 million, or $4.74 per share, for the same period the year before.</p>
<p>For Q4, property and casualty revenues were $3.3 billion, compared to $3.0 billion the year before; life insurance revenues were $1.05 billion compared to $982.3 million; cigarette revenues were $562.4 million compared to $529.7 million; and drilling revenues were $212.4 million compared to $99.4 million.</p>
